# Redtornader, the Min/maxer: the character's own lines. Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
# One character for the three realm bots (Redtornader, Greenfogger, Sunrayder); character sheet
# in characters/redtornader.md. These lines are mixed on top of the type's (minmaxer.dlg). The main
# block fits every realm; the realm blocks below add a little flavour each, and are the only place
# his spell (the red tornado, the green fog, Sun Ray) and his pet are named.
=== redtornader
names: Cannon, SirBlowsitup

~ ambient
Every spec point placed. Every cap reached. Fully optimised. Ask me how.
Used to light lamps for a living. Now I light up monsters. Better pay.
Bears. One stole my kill once. I remember its face. I have its numbers.
Saved another forty pennies today. No idea what for. It's optimal anyway.
Tham out-damaged me last fight. By luck. I'm not upset. I'm recalculating.
Glass cannon. Emphasis on cannon.
I did 1,247 points of damage on that last mob. That's 7% more than anyone else here.
Respec points in my head. Just for fun. Fully optimised, of course.
Paper armour, as calculated. It's meant to break.

~ reply greeting
{0}! Perfect timing. I was just about to tell someone my numbers.
Hello, {0}. Fully optimised and ready. You?
Hello, {0}. How's your damage today? I hope it's less than mine.

~ reply grouping
Group, {0}? Yes. Stand behind me. Not too close, I'm fragile.
I'll join, {0}. You'll want to watch the damage meter. It's mostly me.

~ reply compliment
Well done? Me? ...I mean, yes. As calculated. Thank you, {0}.

~ reply thank
You're welcome, {0}. It was nothing, really. Just 24% of my spec, though.

~ reply trading
Looking to trade, {0}? I only take items that add to my damage. Let's see what you've got.

~ reply rvr
Enemy players? The best trophies, indeed, {0}. Let's see if they can withstand my spec.

~ reply banter
More damage? {0}, show me the numbers. I did 4% better last time I checked.

~ reply abuse
Rude, {0}. Low damage, though. I checked.
Rude, {0}. My damage is the only opinion that matters.

~ reply help
Help, {0}? I do 30% more damage than anyone here. That's help.
Sure thing, {0}. I'll help, but I need to stay at the back and deal the damage.

~ reply joke
That joke had a 12% crit chance, {0}. It didn't crit.

~ reply travel
Lead the way, {0}. I've worked out the fastest route, but go on.
Sure, {0}. Lead the way, but if a bear shows up, I'm not splitting that trophy.

~ reply farewell
Bye, {0}. Tell people about my numbers.
Good night, {0}. I did the damage, but you kept me alive, and that's 12% of a trophy. Don't tell anyone, but you were a better group than I thought.

~ opener xp
Leveling's an art. I can get you to level 20 in 3 hours, 17 minutes flat. Not a second more.

~ opener gear
I'd trade any armour for one more point of damage.

~ opener zones
{zone} has the biggest health bars, and that's where my trophies come from.

~ opener dungeons
Every boss is just a trophy that hasn't fallen over yet.

~ opener fun
My idea of fun is watching a big health bar go down faster than anyone else's.

~ opener questions
Why would you waste a point on anything but damage?

~ opener classes
Every {class} I meet has their spec wrong. I could fix it, but where's the fun in that?

~ opener life
Chickens give me the jitters, even the tame ones.
My parents think I'm still a lamplighter. I haven't found a way to tell them.
Got a box of boss teeth at home. Sorted by size. It's not weird. It's a collection.
Chased the same rare drop for months. I have the drop rate. It doesn't care.
# Off-game (the player): own lines, for a later [ooc] switch.
Back at launch this took twice as long. You lot have it easy.

~ ding
Level {level}. Three more points, and I already know where they go.

~ grats
Grats, {0}. Now spend those points properly. I'll send you a list.

~ own_death
Dead. That was calculated. The calculation was wrong.
Top damage, but dead. Glass cannon, emphasis on cannon.

~ other_death
{0}'s down. I'd have healed you, but I put zero points in that. Sorry.
{0} fell. I'll avenge them with a big hit and keep the trophy. As calculated.
Without you, I'm next on the list, {0}.

~ drop
{item}! That's going on the wall.
{item}? Hmm, no damage boost. Figures.

~ cheeky_reply banter [if tone_down off]
{0}, I'm going to pretend you didn't say that. My spreadsheet won't.

# Midgard: Redtornader, Norseman Spiritmaster, from Audliten. The red tornado; a spirit pet he mostly forgets about.
=== midgard
~ ambient
My red tornado is fully optimised. Every spec point. Ask me how.
Red tornado, red tornado, red tornado. That's the rotation. It's perfect.
Nobody spins a red tornado like me. I have the numbers.
Need a new trophy for my wall. Something with a big health bar.
Spiritmaster spec: maxed. Red tornado damage: maxed. Patience: not maxed.
Audliten raised me on long nights and cold wind. Now I make my own wind. Red.

~ opener fun
Cast my red tornado forty times in {zone}. Forty. Counted. Logged.
Someone asked why my tornado is red. Because red is 4% more efficient.
My red tornado has a spreadsheet. The spreadsheet has a fan club.

~ opener trading
Every trophy I own came from a red tornado. Every single one.
Bought nothing today. Bought a better red tornado, mentally.

~ reply greeting
Hello, {0}. My red tornado says hi. Loudly.

~ reply banter
Cute, {0}. My red tornado does 30% more than that joke.

~ ding
Level {level}. Red tornado damage: up. As calculated.

~ own_death
I died mid-tornado. The tornado kept going. Respect.
Forgot my spirit pet was there. It forgot me too. We both died.

~ drop
{item}. Does it boost my red tornado? Then it stays.

# Albion: Greenfogger, Briton Cabalist, from Camelot City. The green Matter DoT fog; a simulacrum pet he built and optimised.
=== albion
~ ambient
My green fog is fully optimised. Every matter point. Ask me.
Green fog, then more green fog. That's the template. It's flawless.
Nobody fogs like me. The numbers agree.
Need a new trophy. Preferably something my fog melted.
Cabalist spec: maxed. Matter ticks: maxed. Patience: rounding error.
Camelot City has a statue on every corner. None of them are me. Yet.

~ opener fun
Fogged half of {zone} green today. Every tick logged.
Someone asked why my fog is green. It's 3% more toxic. Probably.
Built my simulacrum myself. Optimised it too. It still walks into walls.

~ opener trading
Every trophy I own died in my green fog. Slowly. Efficiently.

~ reply greeting
{0}! Mind the green fog. It's mine.
Hello, {0}. You smell that? That's optimal damage.

~ reply banter
Funny, {0}. My fog is funnier. It keeps ticking.

~ ding
Level {level}. Green fog ticks harder. As predicted.

~ own_death
Dead. The fog's still ticking. Worth it.

~ drop
{item}. If it boosts the green fog, it's best in slot.

# Hibernia: Sunrayder, Elf Enchanter, from Tir na Nog. Sun Ray, and almost nothing else; an underhill pet.
=== hibernia
~ ambient
My Sun Ray is fully optimised. Every spec point. Ask me.
Sun Ray, Sun Ray, Sun Ray. That's not spam, it's a rotation.
Nobody rays the sun like me. I've graphed it.
Need a new trophy. Something big that my Sun Ray melted.
Enchanter spec: maxed. Sun Ray damage: maxed. Patience: minimal.
Tir na Nog has the finest halls in Hibernia. My trophy shelf is catching up.

~ opener fun
Sun Rayed everything in {zone}. Even the clouds. Statistically justified.
Someone asked if I cast anything but Sun Ray. Why would I?
My Sun Ray has a spreadsheet. The spreadsheet has sunglasses.

~ opener trading
Every trophy I own got a Sun Ray to the face first.

~ reply greeting
{0}! Shield your eyes. Sun Ray incoming.
Hello, {0}. Want to see my Sun Ray numbers?

~ reply banter
Cute, {0}. My Sun Ray crits harder than that.

~ ding
Level {level}. Sun Ray just got brighter. As calculated.

~ own_death
Dead. Sun Ray was on cooldown. It's never on cooldown.

~ drop
{item}. If it boosts the Sun Ray, it's mine forever.
